<title>USA: Immune Response over-allotment exercised.</title>
<headline>Immune Response over-allotment exercised.</headline>
<dateline>CARLSBAD, Calif. 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Immune Response Corp said that underwriters in its recently completed public offering of common stock have exercised their over-allotment option and bought another 330,000 shares of its common stock.</p>
<p>As a result, it sold an additional 330,000 shares at the public offering price of $6.50 per share, bringing the net proceeds to $15.4 million.</p>
<p>The option was granted in connection with Immune Response's public offering of 2,200,000 shares in October 1996. All of the shares were sold by the company.</p>
</text>
